<title>SPAIN: FORECAST - Spain CPI consensus sees 0.5 % Aug rise.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Spain CPI consensus sees 0.5 % Aug rise.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a simple average of CPI forecasts contributed by private economists:</p>
<p>	   Mth  Change   Range     Pvs  Yr-yr  Range   96/95  Ave</p>
<p>CPI  (%) Aug  +0.50% (0.3/0.6)   0.1  3.90 (3.7/4.0)  3.58 3.68</p>
<p>Core (%) Aug  +0.30% (0.11/0.60) 0.1  3.69 (3.5/3.9)  3.51 3.77</p>
<p>Sources: Argentaria, AFI, Beta Capital, Banco Santander, BCH, Caja Madrid, BBV, Intermoney, SocGen, BoA, Merrill Lynch, ICAE, BSN, C. Lyonnais, Fedea.</p>
<p>NOTE - The National Statistics Institute will publish the official figure on Sep 13. Core inflation excludes energy and unprocessed food.</p>
</text>
